    <strong>What to notice:</strong> each question hides a trap the sections warned about — the
    bottle that looks like contract, the arithmetic that answers against the precaution, the
    skull nobody could foresee, the disease nobody can attribute. Commit to an answer first,
    then read the feedback as a verdict with reasons; if the Hand question tripped you, redo
    the worked example until it feels mechanical.
  </p>

